{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01XPGpeyNbMkXu9vYCDqZZyW","type":"tool_result","content":"1:# Pixel Engine API (v0.46.0)\n5:## Sections\n23:## 1. Engine and games\n25:### ADAPTIVE_ASPECT\n33:### type AspectMode\n39:### BUILTIN_MODELS\n47:### chunkyResolution()\n55:### clearScene()\n63:### computeFraming()\n69:### countObjects()\n77:### type DebugAction\n87:### type DebugKeyChanges\n95:### type DebugKeyMap\n101:### type DebugKeysOption\n114:### DEFAULT_DEBUG_KEYS\n122:### disposeObject()\n132:### class Engine\n197:### ENGINE_VERSION\n203:### interface EngineOptions\n226:### FPS_OPTIONS\n232:### class FrameLimiter\n242:### frameView()\n253:### interface Framing\n266:### interface Game\n288:### interface GameContext\n305:### interface HeadlessOptions\n312:### class LoadingScreen\n323:### loadSettings()\n331:### normalizeSettings()\n339:### optionsFromUrl()\n352:### PIXEL_SIZES\n358:### interface PlayerSettings\n372:### QUALITY\n381:### QUALITY_LEVELS\n387:### QUALITY_OPTIONS\n393:### type QualityLevel\n407:### type QualityOption\n413:### interface QualitySettings\n418:### rebindDebugKeys()\n428:### interface Resolution\n446:### RESOLUTIONS\n452:### resolveDebugKeys()\n460:### class Settings\n479:### interface SettingsHost\n492:### class SettingsPanel\n507:### storeSettings()\n513:### urlSettings()\n523:### interface Viewport\n531:### withUrlOptions()\n542:## 2. Camera\n544:### CAMERA_PRESETS\n550:### interface CameraConfig\n566:### type CameraPreset\n577:### class CameraRig\n604:### interface CameraRigState\n617:### createCameraRig()\n623:### class FirstPersonRig\n637:### class FreeRig\n655:### class OrthoRig\n666:### class ThirdPersonRig\n677:## 3. Rendering, looks and filters\n679:### AMOUNT\n687:### applyFilter()\n696:### applyFilters()\n704:### type BackendName\n712:### interface CapturedFrame\n718:### clampParam()\n726:### cloneLook()\n732:### DEFAULT_EDGES\n738:### DEFAULT_PIXEL\n744:### defaultLook()\n752:### defaultParams()\n760:### interface EdgeSettings\n765:### FILTER_IDS\n771:### FILTER_PRESETS\n779:### interface FilterContext\n786:### interface FilterDef\n798:### type FilterGroup\n804:### filterOrder()\n812:### interface FilterParam\n824:### filterParams()\n832:### filterPresetOf()\n842:### filterPresets()\n850:### FILTERS\n856:### type FilterSpace\n862:### getFilter()\n868:### interface LayerLook\n875:### interface Look\n881:### LOOK_ALIASES\n889:### LOOK_PRESETS\n899:### LOOK_TARGET_LABELS\n905:### LOOK_TARGETS\n911:### interface LookFilter\n918:### lookFilters()\n926:### lookFromFilters()\n934:### type LookLayer\n942:### lookLayerOf()\n950:### interface LookPlan\n957:### lookPresetLabel()\n965:### lookPresetName()\n973:### lookPresetOf()\n981:### looksEqual()\n987:### type LookTarget\n995:### NO_WEBGPU\n1003:### normalizeLook()\n1013:### PALETTES\n1019:### paramsOf()\n1027:### PIXEL_PARAMS\n1033:### PIXEL_PRESETS\n1039:### interface PixelLook\n1047:### class PixelRenderer\n1103:### planLook()\n1112:### type RenderMode\n1118:### scenePixel()\n1126:### setLookLayer()\n1136:### splitFilters()\n1146:## 4. Materials, meshes and lights\n1148:### interface AssignItem\n1159:### class ContactShadow\n1169:### flicker()\n1178:### FLICKER_PRESETS\n1184:### type FlickerPreset\n1192:### glowMaterial()\n1203:### LIGHT_POOL_SIZES\n1211:### class LightAssigner\n1227:### interface LightHandle\n1249:### class LightPool\n1267:### interface LightPoolOptions\n1272:### interface LightPoolStats\n1281:### interface LightRequestOptions\n1297:### interface MergeOptions\n1302:### mergeStaticMeshes()\n1319:### PALETTE\n1329:### type PaletteColor\n1335:### pixelTexture()\n1343:### TOON_BANDS\n1352:### toonGradient()\n1358:### toonify()\n1368:### toonMaterial()\n1380:### interface ToonMaterialOptions\n1387:## 5. Physics\n1389:### interface BoxOptions\n1397:### interface Breakable\n1404:### interface BreakableOptions\n1417:### class Breakables\n1431:### interface BridgeOptions\n1441:### interface Built\n1448:### chain()\n1460:### interface ChainOptions\n1470:### type CharacterAnim\n# Pixel Engine 0.46.0\n\nA WebGPU engine that renders 3D scenes as authentic pixel art (WebGPU only), with\nRapier physics, a platformer character with a full animation set, pixel HUD, audio, particles\nand a look system (filters per layer). This folder is everything a game needs.\n\nRead in this order:\n\n1. `GUIDE.md` (~15k tokens): how to host a game, the mental model, a complete game, recipes, the rules and common mistakes. Read it whole.\n2. `API.md` (~62k tokens): every export with its signature and doc. Search it; don't read it whole.\n3. `game.js`: the guide's quick start, a complete game. Edit it into yours.\n4. `ASSETS.md` (~4k tokens), when the game builds with models and textures: the library, the format, the loop and the style rules. Read it whole; `LIBRARY.md` (~44k tokens) lists every model and texture, built in or from a pack: search it (or filter `library.json`).\n\n| File | What |\n| --- | --- |\n| `pixel-engine.js` | The engine, 4750 KB: one ES module with three.js (`THREE`, `TSL`), Rapier and its wasm, the hero kit, the built-in models (`assets/coin.glb`, `assets/hero.glb`, `assets/tree.glb`) and the engine CSS. Never edit it. |\n| `index.html`, `game.js` | A game to start from: serve this folder over HTTP and open `index.html` |\n| `examples/` | The guides' other recipes as pages (`side-scroller`, `top-down`, `looks`, `market`) and the modules they import (`market-models.js`) |\n| `check.mjs` | `node check.mjs [page] [--keys KeyD*60,Space*4] [--cameras] [--looks a,b]`: plays the page in a real browser, saves screenshots, fails on any error. Run it before you hand a game back. `node check.mjs --headless game.js` plays the game in Node with no browser and replays it (GUIDE.md section 8); `node check.mjs --sheets models.js` draws your models and textures (ASSETS.md) |\n| `ASSETS.md`, `LIBRARY.md`, `CREDITS.md` | Models and textures as data; the built-in library and the imported packs, by family; where everything the kit carries came from (ship it with your game) |\n| `library.json` | Every model and texture as data (id, kind, family, pack, tags, size, licence): filter it to find what a game needs |\n| `packs/` | Imported packs (`packs/index.json` lists them): `loadPack('packs/<id>.json')` |\n| `pixel-engine.d.ts`, `types/` | TypeScript declarations (optional) |\n| `CHANGELOG.md` | What changed between engine versions |\n| `LICENSE` | The engine's licence (MIT) |\n| `manifest.json` | Version, build, where newer versions are (`latest`, `releases`, `source`) and every file with its size |\n\nServe it: `npx serve .` or `python3 -m http.server` here, then open http://localhost:3000/ (or :8000).\nES modules don't load from `file://`.\n\nNewer versions: the newest release of the kit is always https://github.com/michaelcrosato/riftlight/releases/latest/download/pixel-engine.zip, and every release stays\nat https://github.com/michaelcrosato/riftlight/releases with what changed in it. To build one from\nthe engine's repository instead: `git clone --depth 1 https://github.com/michaelcrosato/riftlight && cd riftlight && npm ci && npm run bundle`\nmakes `bundle/pixel-engine/`. To upgrade a game, see GUIDE.md, section 10.\n// Coin Garden: walk (WASD / arrows / stick), jump (Space), collect every coin.\nimport { compileClips, ContactShadow, Engine, HERO_CLIPS, HERO_MODEL, HERO_RIG, mergeStaticMeshes, PlatformerCharacter, readMoveInput, setLookLayer, THREE, toonMaterial, withUrlOptions } from './pixel-engine.js';\n\nconst { BoxGeometry, Mesh, Vector3 } = THREE;\n\n<!doctype html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n  <head>\n    <meta charset=\"utf-8\" />\n    <meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1, maximum-scale=1, user-scalable=no, viewport-fit=cover\" />\n    <link rel=\"icon\" href=\"data:,\" />\n    <title>Pixel Engine game</title>\n    <style>html, body { margin: 0; height: 100%; background: #0d0b14; } #app { position: fixed; inset: 0; }</style>\n  </head>\n  <body>\n    <div id=\"app\"></div>\n    <script type=\"module\" src=\"./game.js\"></script>\n  </body>\n</html>","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"71ec49de-27ff-45fb-a784-9f3cf302f915","uuid":"37c31a14-a87c-4154-9d27-910a94ee4937","timestamp":"2026-11-05T23:21:16.910Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"1:# Pixel Engine API (v0.46.0)\n5:## Sections\n23:## 1. Engine and games\n25:### ADAPTIVE_ASPECT\n33:### type AspectMode\n39:### BUILTIN_MODELS\n47:### chunkyResolution()\n55:### clearScene()\n63:### computeFraming()\n69:### countObjects()\n77:### type DebugAction\n87:### type DebugKeyChanges\n95:### type DebugKeyMap\n101:### type DebugKeysOption\n114:### DEFAULT_DEBUG_KEYS\n122:### disposeObject()\n132:### class Engine\n197:### ENGINE_VERSION\n203:### interface EngineOptions\n226:### FPS_OPTIONS\n232:### class FrameLimiter\n242:### frameView()\n253:### interface Framing\n266:### interface Game\n288:### interface GameContext\n305:### interface HeadlessOptions\n312:### class LoadingScreen\n323:### loadSettings()\n331:### normalizeSettings()\n339:### optionsFromUrl()\n352:### PIXEL_SIZES\n358:### interface PlayerSettings\n372:### QUALITY\n381:### QUALITY_LEVELS\n387:### QUALITY_OPTIONS\n393:### type QualityLevel\n407:### type QualityOption\n413:### interface QualitySettings\n418:### rebindDebugKeys()\n428:### interface Resolution\n446:### RESOLUTIONS\n452:### resolveDebugKeys()\n460:### class Settings\n479:### interface SettingsHost\n492:### class SettingsPanel\n507:### storeSettings()\n513:### urlSettings()\n523:### interface Viewport\n531:### withUrlOptions()\n542:## 2. Camera\n544:### CAMERA_PRESETS\n550:### interface CameraConfig\n566:### type CameraPreset\n577:### class CameraRig\n604:### interface CameraRigState\n617:### createCameraRig()\n623:### class FirstPersonRig\n637:### class FreeRig\n655:### class OrthoRig\n666:### class ThirdPersonRig\n677:## 3. Rendering, looks and filters\n679:### AMOUNT\n687:### a