{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01LX1URDUEJJcM7aziAPKfLx","type":"tool_result","content":"--- STAGE.md\nBuild the game PLAN.md describes. Take your file names and what to hand in from TASK.md, which is filled in for you. Keep your progress in PROGRESS.md, so you can pick up where you were after your context is compacted.\n--- TASK.md, deliverable and hand-in lines\n11:Package: For ease of deployment and sharing provide a single html file [GameTitle-SOURCE-claude-opus-5-5-xhigh-20261105-162027].html. Dependencies that can be downloaded do not have to be included in the html file if that is easier.\n23:Working Environment and deliverable:\n24:Create a subfolder called [GameTitle-SOURCE-claude-opus-5-5-xhigh-20261105-162027] to keep all your dev files in. You can develop separate modules, then bundle into a single file [GameTitle-SOURCE-claude-opus-5-5-xhigh-20261105-162027].html in root when you\n50:No script can check these, so they're written by hand. Test with the stand-ins; anything that needs the real thing is checked as far as it can be here, never required.\n52:- **No physical controller.** Emulate one: replace navigator.getGamepads with a stub that returns a pad in the standard mapping (Playwright's add_init_script / addInitScript).\n53:- **No touch device.** Use Playwright's phone and tablet profiles, which have touch, and tap with page.touchscreen.\n54:- **Nobody to listen.** Check sound by what Web Audio produces: render it with an OfflineAudioContext, or read levels from an AnalyserNode.\n55:- **No second player.** Play multiplayer with two browser pages (or contexts) on this computer.\n56:- **No real iPhone or iPad.** WebKit with an iPhone profile is the closest; it isn't iOS Safari.\n57:- **No TV.** Judge the 10-foot view from screenshots at 1920×1080.\n93:CRITICAL: Put Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback and Prompt Feedback in your chat reply and an in-game About/Credits screen. Write \"unknown\" for anything you can't confirm.\n109:Exit interview: before you finish, also save these answers as exit-interview.json in this folder's root, beside the game's .html: one JSON object in exactly the shape below, every value filled in (\"unknown\" for anything you can't confirm). Tools read it (t\n--- step types the plan names vs built\n603:**Step types:** `goto leave talk report use deliver destroy kill collect steal hold escort ride timer choice script`. A step shows its `text` for 5 s at the top when it starts, and always in the m\ngoto leave talk report use deliver enter destroy blast kill collect hold timer choice script \n--- plan-named items, used or not\nHolster: 1\nmuffle: 1\nshifter: 0\nstone-wall: 0\nbattlement: 0\n0\nsrc/ui/screens","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"71ec49de-27ff-45fb-a784-9f3cf302f915","uuid":"3bbc779b-9634-4ad6-8ca7-79c7f5c1e3ea","timestamp":"2026-11-06T02:49:21.749Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"--- STAGE.md\nBuild the game PLAN.md describes. Take your file names and what to hand in from TASK.md, which is filled in for you. Keep your progress in PROGRESS.md, so you can pick up where you were after your context is compacted.\n--- TASK.md, deliverable and hand-in lines\n11:Package: For ease of deployment and sharing provide a single html file [GameTitle-SOURCE-claude-opus-5-5-xhigh-20261105-162027].html. Dependencies that can be downloaded do not have to be included in the html file if that is easier.\n23:Working Environment and deliverable:\n24:Create a subfolder called [GameTitle-SOURCE-claude-opus-5-5-xhigh-20261105-162027] to keep all your dev files in. You can develop separate modules, then bundle into a single file [GameTitle-SOURCE-claude-opus-5-5-xhigh-20261105-162027].html in root when you\n50:No script can check these, so they're written by hand. Test with the stand-ins; anything that needs the real thing is checked as far as it can be here, never required.\n52:- **No physical controller.** Emulate one: replace navigator.getGamepads with a stub that returns a pad in the standard mapping (Playwright's add_init_script / addInitScript).\n53:- **No touch device.** Use Playwright's phone and tablet profiles, which have touch, and tap with page.touchscreen.\n54:- **Nobody to listen.** Check sound by what Web Audio produces: render it with an OfflineAudioContext, or read levels from an AnalyserNode.\n55:- **No second player.** Play multiplayer with two browser pages (or contexts) on this computer.\n56:- **No real iPhone or iPad.** WebKit with an iPhone profile is the closest; it isn't iOS Safari.\n57:- **No TV.** Judge the 10-foot view from screenshots at 1920×1080.\n93:CRITICAL: Put Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback and Prompt Feedback in your chat reply and an in-game About/Credits screen. Write \"unknown\" for anything you can't confirm.\n109:Exit interview: before you finish, also save these answers as exit-interview.json in this folder's root, beside the game's .html: one JSON object in exactly the shape below, every value filled in (\"unknown\" for anything you can't confirm). Tools read it (t\n--- step types the plan names vs built\n603:**Step types:** `goto leave talk report use deliver destroy kill collect steal hold escort ride timer choice script`. A step shows its `text` for 5 s at the top when it starts, and always in the m\ngoto leave talk report use deliver enter destroy blast kill collect hold timer choice script \n--- plan-named items, used or not\nHolster: 1\nmuffle: 1\nshifter: 0\nstone-wall: 0\nbattlement: 0\n0\nsrc/ui/screens","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01LX1URDUEJJcM7aziAPKfLx","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
