{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01LG8HbGFFF3RHhS3pTqHDXB","type":"tool_result","content":"1:// Getting in and out, the cab, the wheel in your hands, the map at speed, the chase camera, the mounted gun, the bonnet.\n28:      this.cab = buildModel(cabHands);\n29:      setLookLayer(this.cab.object, 'actors');\n30:      this.cab.object.traverse((o) => { if (o.isMesh) { o.castShadow = false; o.frustumCulled = false; } });\n31:      this.cabWheel = this.cab.object.getObjectByName('Wheel');\n32:      this.cabArrow = this.cab.object.getObjectByName('DashArrow');\n33:      this.cabRest = this.cabWheel.rotation.z;\n34:      this.cabShifter = this.cab.object.getObjectByName('Shifter');\n35:      this.cabArm = this.cab.object.getObjectByName('ArmShift');\n36:      this.cabGrip = this.cab.object.getObjectByName('GripR');\n38:      this.cab.object.visible = false;\n39:      ctx.scene.add(this.cab.object);\n189:    if (g.views) { g.vehicles.cab.object.visible = true; v.object.add(g.vehicles.cab.object); const s = v.def.seat; g.vehicles.cab.object.position.set(s[0], s[1], s[2]); }\n220:    if (g.views) { g.vehicles.cab.object.visible = false; g.ctx.scene.add(g.vehicles.cab.object); }\n235:          if (g.views) g.vehicles.cab.object.visible = false;\n240:          if (g.views) g.vehicles.cab.object.visible = true;\n272:      const cab = g.vehicles;\n273:      if (cab.cabWheel) { cab.cabWheel.rotation.z = cab.cabRest + this.steer * 1.4; }\n279:      cab.cabArm.position.set(cab.cabArmRest.x - k * 0.08, cab.cabArmRest.y + (1 - k) * 0.12, cab.cabArmRest.z + (1 - k) * 0.02 - k * 0.02);\n280:      cab.cabGrip.visible = k < 0.15;\n281:      cab.cabShifter.rotation.x = k * 0.4 * (this.shiftDir ?? 1);\n282:      if (cab.cabArrow && g.map.waypoint) { const want = Math.atan2(g.map.waypoint[0] - v.x, g.map.waypoint[1] - v.z); cab.cabArrow.rotation.y = wrapAngle(want - v.yaw); }\n289:      if (g.views) g.vehicles.cab.object.visible = false;\n290:    } else if (g.cam.override && !g.scene.active) { g.cam.override = null; if (g.views && !this.gunning) g.vehicles.cab.object.visible = true; }\ngs: ['first-person', 'vehicle'], floats: true, collider: 'none', palette: { wheel: 'ink', hub: 'night', sleeve: 'night', skin: 'plum', dash: 'plum', dial: 'sand', arrow: 'lime' },\n915:- Tablet to mouth, syrette, **four surgery scenes**, **raise map** and tracker, monocular, wrench on bonnet, hand on wheel and shifter, finish-it.\n| `stone-wall` | 2 × 3 × 0.3 | length 2 (0.5–6), height 3 (0.5–5) | stone mist, stone2 slate, mortar night | architecture, stone, wall, modular | Modular stone wall along X, `length` x 0.3 m centred on the origin, `height` 3 m to a storey: blocks in two shaded courses over dark mortar (one course alternates its blocks); its ends meet the next piece so the bond runs on across pieces set end to end on the 1 m grid |\n| `battlement` | 3 × 1.83 × 0.42 | merlons 3 (1–8) | stone mist, stone2 slate, mortar night, dressed sand, slit ink | architecture, stone, wall, castle, modular | Crenellated parapet to sit on a wall top (y = 0 there): a dressed string course, a coursed breast wall and coping, `merlons` slit merlons one to each metre with half a crenel at each end so pieces line up; footprint `merlons` x 0.42 m |\n154:- `readonly qualityOption: QualityOption`: Requested quality (`auto` adapts); `quality` is the level in use.\n163:- `get lights: LightPool`: The dynamic light pool (render/lights.ts), engine-owned: its lights stay in the scene across levels, so loading another level never changes the light count (no recompiles). Created on first use; sized by quality.\n169:- `get quality: QualityLevel`: The quality level in use (see `EngineOptions.quality`).\n302:- `readonly lights: LightPool`: Dynamic point lights: `lights.request({ position, color, intensity, radius, flicker })` (src/engine/render/lights.ts). A fixed pool sized by quality, created on first use.\n425:use for a key does at runtime (`engine.debugK