{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgkvj7EeT9xPiGMvbx7MN","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_017JsWQKXnqG6FgUTXVoUKN2","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"sed -n 80,100p ASSETS.md | cut -c1-420\ngrep -n \"collider\\b.*parts\\|collide: false\\|'parts'\" ASSETS.md | head -8 | cut -c1-320\nsed -n 268,283p src/vehicles/driving.js | cut -c1-200\nsed -n 1,10p src/vehicles/driving.js | cut -c1-140\ngrep -n \"tris\\|budget\" tests/suites/static.mjs | head -6 | cut -c1-200\ngrep -n \"cab-hands\\|cabHands\\|forceViews\" tests/suites/*.mjs tests/lib/bot.mjs | head -8 | cut -c1-200","description":"Read use and collider docs and the cab update code"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2753,"cache_read_input_tokens":65766,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2753},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"71ec49de-27ff-45fb-a784-9f3cf302f915","uuid":"343c47e3-dc22-46aa-9126-f1b6843708f8","timestamp":"2026-11-06T03:00:56.116Z","request_id":"req_011Cgkvj6t4Jp7GyHw7z39J7","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_017JsWQKXnqG6FgUTXVoUKN2":{"command":"sed -n 80,100p ASSETS.md | cut -c1-420\ngrep -n \"collider\\b.*parts\\|collide: false\\|'parts'\" ASSETS.md | head -8 | cut -c1-320\nsed -n 268,283p src/vehicles/driving.js | cut -c1-200\nsed -n 1,10p src/vehicles/driving.js | cut -c1-140\ngrep -n \"tris\\|budget\" tests/suites/static.mjs | head -6 | cut -c1-200\ngrep -n \"cab-hands\\|cabHands\\|forceViews\" tests/suites/*.mjs tests/lib/bot.mjs | head -8 | cut -c1-200","description":"Read use and collider docs and the cab update code"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_017JsWQKXnqG6FgUTXVoUKN2","type":"tool_result","content":"**Composition:**\n\n- `{ group: [...], at, rot, scale, c }`: a frame whose `c` is its parts' default. `pivot: true`\n  with a `name` keeps it a movable Group (a door, a lid: `build.object.getObjectByName('lid')`).\n- `{ mirror: [...], axis: 'x' }`: the parts and their mirror image (`axis: 'z'` mirrors front to back).\n- `{ use: 'barrel', at, rot, scale, params, seed, palette: { theirs: 'ours' } }`: another model\n  by id. Its slots map onto yours through `palette`, else onto yours of the same name, else keep\n  their own colours.\n- `on: 'name'`: sit on the named part's top; `at` becomes an offset from there.\n- `params: { h: [default, min, max] }` with `parts: (p, rng) => [...]`: parametric (`p.h`) and\n  seeded (`rng.range(a, b)`). Helpers return parts: `around`, `rowOf`, `gridOf`, `scatterOf`,\n  `boxFrame`.\n- Model keys: `size` (declared bounds, checked), `anchors` (`{ grip: [x, y, z] }`), `light: { at,\n  c, intensity, radius, flicker }`, `collider` (`'box'`, `'cyl'`, `'hull'`, `'parts'` (a box per\n  part: doorways stay open) or `'none'`), `floats: true` (it hangs), `texel` (texels a metre for\n  `tex` parts, default 8).\n\n**Problems** (`check.mjs --sheets` exits 1; `buildModel` throws a `ModelError` on those it can't\nbuild): no `about` or `tags`; an undeclared slot or a colour that isn't a palette name; an unknown\n`use`, `on` or texture; a size that isn't positive; `seg` outside 3–64; NaN; an empty model; below\nthe floor (unless `floats`); over the declared `size`; params out of range; a part that both\n77:  heart, eyes), `tex` (a texture id, section 3), `seg` and `collide: false` (no box of its own\n78:  under `collider: 'parts'`: a doorway's mortar ring).\n93:  c, intensity, radius, flicker }`, `collider` (`'box'`, `'cyl'`, `'hull'`, `'parts'` (a box per\n    const speed = Math.abs(v.car.speed);\n    if (this.engine) this.engine.set({ volume: v.stalled ? 0 : 0.28 + clamp(speed / 26, 0, 1) * 0.3, pitch: -6 + clamp(speed / 26, 0, 1) * 16 - (v.hp < 35 ? 2 : 0) });\n    if (g.actions.tapped('sprint')) g.sfx.play('horn', { volume: 0.8 });\n    if (g.views) {\n      const cab = g.vehicles;\n      if (cab.cabWheel) { cab.cabWheel.rotation.z = cab.cabRest + this.steer * 1.4; }\n      // Through the gears: the right hand leaves the wheel for the lever and back.\n      const gear = Math.floor(speed / 7);\n      if (gear !== this.gear) { if (this.gear != null) { this.shiftT = 0.5; this.shiftDir = gear > this.gear ? 1 : -1; g.sfx.play('gun-mag', { volume: 0.25, pitch: -8 }); } this.gear = gear; }\n      this.shiftT = Math.max(0, (this.shiftT ?? 0) - dt);\n      const k = Math.sin(Math.min(1, this.shiftT / 0.5) * Math.PI);\n      cab.cabArm.position.set(cab.cabArmRest.x - k * 0.08, cab.cabArmRest.y + (1 - k) * 0.12, cab.cabArmRest.z + (1 - k) * 0.02 - k * 0.02);\n      cab.cabGrip.visible = k < 0.15;\n      cab.cabShifter.rotation.x = k * 0.4 * (this.shiftDir ?? 1);\n      if (cab.cabArrow && g.map.waypoint) { const want = Math.atan2(g.map.waypoint[0] - v.x, g.map.waypoint[1] - v.z); cab.cabArrow.rotation.y = wrapAngle(want - v.yaw); }\n    }\n// Getting in and out, the cab, the wheel in your hands, the map at speed, the chase camera, the mounted gun, the bonnet.\nimport { THREE, buildModel, setLookLayer, spatialize } from '../../pixel-engine.js';\nimport { TUNING } from '../core/tuning.js';\nimport { cabHands } from '../art/viewmodels.js';\nimport { Vehicle2, KINDS } from './vehicle.js';\nimport { ROADS } from '../content/roads.js';\nimport { pointAlong, polyLength } from '../world/ground.js';\nimport { makePerson } from '../actors/rig.js';\nimport { clamp, lerp, wrapAngle } from '../core/rng.js';\nconst { Vector3, Quaternion, Group } = THREE;\ntests/suites/static.mjs:49:  const { handsDef, cabHands, rackDefs, HANDS_CLIPS, HANDS_RIG } = await import('../../src/art/viewmodels.js');\ntests/suites/static.mjs:50:  for (const d of [...OWN_MODELS, handsDef, cabHands, ...Object.values(rackDefs)]) { const r = checkModel(d, { catalog: MODELS }); t.ok(`model ${d.id}`, r.problems.length ==\ntests/suites/soak.mjs:13:  const { game: g, engine: e } = await boot({ forceViews: true, seed });\ntests/suites/playthrough.mjs:10:    const { game: g, engine: e } = await boot({ seed: variant.length, forceViews: variant.includes('alone') });","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"71ec49de-27ff-45fb-a784-9f3cf302f915","uuid":"c594256f-6408-4436-9f44-5ced8f68b9af","timestamp":"2026-11-06T03:00:56.180Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"**Composition:**\n\n- `{ group: [...], at, rot, scale, c }`: a frame whose `c` is its parts' default. `pivot: true`\n  with a `name` keeps it a movable Group (a door, a lid: `build.object.getObjectByName('lid')`).\n- `{ mirror: [...], axis: 'x' }`: the parts and their mirror image (`axis: 'z'` mirrors front to back).\n- `{ use: 'barrel', at, rot, scale, params, seed, palette: { theirs: 'ours' } }`: another model\n  by id. Its slots map onto yours through `palette`, else onto yours of the same name, else keep\n  their own colours.\n- `on: 'name'`: sit on the named part's top; `at` becomes an offset from there.\n- `params: { h: [default, min, max] }` with `parts: (p, rng) => [...]`: parametric (`p.h`) and\n  seeded (`rng.range(a, b)`). Helpers return parts: `around`, `rowOf`, `gridOf`, `scatterOf`,\n  `boxFrame`.\n- Model keys: `size` (declared bounds, checked), `anchors` (`{ grip: [x, y, z] }`), `light: { at,\n  c, intensity, radius, flicker }`, `collider` (`'box'`, `'cyl'`, `'hull'`, `'parts'` (a box per\n  part: doorways stay open) or `'none'`), `floats: true` (it hangs), `texel` (texels a metre for\n  `tex` parts, default 8).\n\n**Problems** (`check.mjs --sheets` exits 1; `buildModel` throws a `ModelError` on those it can't\nbuild): no `about` or `tags`; an undeclared slot or a colour that isn't a palette name; an unknown\n`use`, `o