{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01ELniT1f53DXKLF5ST3YhxA","type":"tool_result","content":"[98] | Default pad mapping presses keyboard codes (R2 = KeyC, Square = KeyJ...) | Replace `input.gamepadButtons` with `Pad*` codes (below). `isDown`, `wasPressed` and `consumePress` then work on them and keep the devices apart |\n[99] | Right stick arrives as `input.mouseDelta` at `gamepadLookSpeed` (500) px/s, 0.0025 rad per unit | Keep that path so recordings still work. Scale by device in your `step` |\n[151] **Flames.** The library's `fire-burst` is an explosion ring, not grass fire. Write your own strip. In `textureDef`, `size` is the whole strip, frames are equal slices, and each frame's `pixels` layer is placed with `at:[i*w,0]`:\n[204] - `spriteSheet`, `textureMap`, `buildModel` and the HUD all work in Node. Only `drawSheet` needs a canvas: don't use it.\n[345]   - `windFactor = clamp(1 + TUNING.windEffect * windSpeed/5 * 1.6 * cos(angle between neighbour direction and wind), 0.15, 3.5)`\n[346]   - `slopeFactor` = 1.4 uphill, 0.7 downhill. `rainFactor` = 0.15 while raining. `fuelFactor`: grass 1, scrub 0.8, tree 0.6, building 0.4.\n[740] **Touch-only devices.** Detect with `matchMedia('(pointer: coarse)').matches && !matchMedia('(any-pointer: fine)').matches` and no pad connected (verified: true on Chromium with the `iPhone 14`, `iPad Pro 11` and `Pixel 7` profiles, false on a desktop context). Engine option `touch:false` always, so there are never on-screen controls. On such a device the title shows **Controller or keyboard required** (the exact text in `state().notice`, drawn uppercase by the font) and one large **Settings** button (tap works as click: `input.buttonEvents` reports a finger as code `Touch`). Attract mode still starts after 10 s; a tap exits to this\n[872] **Fallback.** If shared-world can't be made stable, ship `ghost` (each copy its own world, others' mercs shown, `progress` and `result` by score, `Math.random` seeded for you) rather than drop multiplayer, and last of all `parallel`.\n[985] `withUrlOptions` keeps the review flags (`?seed=`, `?debug=1`, `?look=`), which are useful and harmless. `debugKeys:false` keeps the engine's R, P and M hotkeys from colliding with yours; dev mode has its own tools.\n---\n28:  raining = false;\n49:      // A fire cell takes the fuel the most of its four terrain cells have.\n102:    const rain = this.raining ? 0.15 : 1;\n121:        let p = 0.02 * FUEL_FACTOR[fuel[nid]] * wf * sf * rain * spread;\n126:      if (ws > 6 && rng.next() < 0.004 * rain * spread) {\n141:    const { defaultBrowserType, ...iphone } = devices['iPhone 14'];\n163:    const { defaultBrowserType, ...iphone } = devices['iPhone 14'];\n### analyzeClip()\n\n```ts\nfunction analyzeClip(model: Object3D, rig: RigSpec, def: ClipDef, clip: AnimationClip): ClipReport\n```\n\n### interface ClipDef\n\n18:12. Animation toolkit: `analyzeClip`, `ClipDef`, `ClipReport`, `compileClip`, `compileClips`, `Foot`, `FootGoal`, `gaitClip`, `gaitPartners`, `GaitSpec`, `Key`, `LegDef`, `LegStepper`, `LegStepperOptions`, `mirror`, `placeFeet`, `Pose`, `renderCurves`, `ren\n3844:### validateClip()\n3847:function validateClip(clip: ClipDef, rig: RigSpec): string[]","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"71ec49de-27ff-45fb-a784-9f3cf302f915","uuid":"36b84fb4-011b-4f09-a776-afc85edaa499","timestamp":"2026-11-06T03:16:35.331Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"[98] | Default pad mapping presses keyboard codes (R2 = KeyC, Square = KeyJ...) | Replace `input.gamepadButtons` with `Pad*` codes (below). `isDown`, `wasPressed` and `consumePress` then work on them and keep the devices apart |\n[99] | Right stick arrives as `input.mouseDelta` at `gamepadLookSpeed` (500) px/s, 0.0025 rad per unit | Keep that path so recordings still work. Scale by device in your `step` |\n[151] **Flames.** The library's `fire-burst` is an explosion ring, not grass fire. Write your own strip. In `textureDef`, `size` is the whole strip, frames are equal slices, and each frame's `pixels` layer is placed with `at:[i*w,0]`:\n[204] - `spriteSheet`, `textureMap`, `buildModel` and the HUD all work in Node. Only `drawSheet` needs a canvas: don't use it.\n[345]   - `windFactor = clamp(1 + TUNING.windEffect * windSpeed/5 * 1.6 * cos(angle between neighbour direction and wind), 0.15, 3.5)`\n[346]   - `slopeFactor` = 1.4 uphill, 0.7 downhill. `rainFactor` = 0.15 while raining. `fuelFactor`: grass 1, scrub 0.8, tree 0.6, building 0.4.\n[740] **Touch-only devices.** Detect with `matchMedia('(pointer: coarse)').matches && !matchMedia('(any-pointer: fine)').matches` and no pad connected (verified: true on Chromium with the `iPhone 14`, `iPad Pro 11` and `Pixel 7` profiles, false on a desktop context). Engine option `touch:false` always, so there are never on-screen controls. On such a device the title shows **Controller or keyboard required** (the exact text in `state().notice`, drawn uppercase by the font) and one large **Settings** button (tap works as click: `input.buttonEvents` reports a finger as code `Touch`). Attract mode still starts after 10 s; a tap exits to this\n[872] **Fallback.** If shared-world can't be made stable, ship `ghost` (each copy its own world, others' mercs shown, `progress` and `result` by score, `Math.random` seeded for you) rather than drop multiplayer, and last of all `parallel`.\n[985] `withUrlOptions` keeps the review flags (`?seed=`, `?debug=1`, `?look=`), which are useful and harmless. `debugKeys:false` keeps the engine's R, P and M hotkeys from colliding with yours; dev mode has its own tools.\n---\n28:  raining = false;\n49:      // A fire cell takes the fuel the most of its four terrain cells have.\n102:    const rain = this.raining ? 0.15 : 1;\n121:        let p = 0.02 * FUEL_FACTOR[fuel[nid]] * wf * sf * rain * spread;\n126:      if (ws > 6 && rng.next() < 0.004 * rain * spread) {\n141:    const { defaultBrowserType, ...iphone } = devices['iPhone 14'];\n163:    const { defaultBrowserType, ...iphone } = devices['iPhone 14'];\n### analyzeClip()\n\n```ts\nfunction analyzeClip(model: Object3D, rig: RigSpec, def: ClipDef, clip: AnimationClip): ClipReport\n```\n\n### interface ClipDef\n\n18:12. Animation toolkit: `analyzeClip`, `ClipDef`, `ClipReport`, `compileClip`, `compileClips`, `Foot`, `FootGoal`, `gaitClip`, `gaitPartners`, `GaitSpec`, `Key`, `LegDef`, `LegStepper`, `LegStepperOptions`, `mirror`, `placeFeet`, `Pose`, `renderCurves`, `ren\n3844:### validateClip()\n3847:function validateClip(clip: ClipDef, rig: RigSpec): string[]","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01ELniT1f53DXKLF5ST3YhxA","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
