{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgkxfX7D1TydZCbAvJZuj","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_011YtEbMBRps4jd643TXvKM1","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"set -e\npython3 - <<'EOF'\ns=open('src/content/about.js').read()\nfor a,b in [\n(\"A stand-in pad, phone profile, two pages for a second player, all four hub scenarios. Screenshots only for what a script cannot check. No review subagents.\",\n \"The engine's own check tool and model sheets. A stand-in pad, phone and tablet profiles, a WebKit iPhone check, two pages for a second player, all four hub scenarios. Screenshots only for what a script cannot check. No review subagents.\"),\n(\"Second was a random-input soak with views on, which found a chase camera crash no script reached.\",\n \"Second was a random-input soak with views on, which found a chase camera crash no script reached. The engine's clip checker earned its place too: run late, it found nine of my clips through the floor.\"),\n(\"I also guessed wrong that one body part of the hands could stay a sibling of the gun, and rebuilt that rig.\",\n \"I also guessed wrong that one body part of the hands could stay a sibling of the gun, and rebuilt that rig. A torus size is a diameter, so a whole steering wheel and the hands on it sat out of frame. And collide: false on a nested model does not reach its parts, so one wall made over 4,000 physics boxes.\"),\n]:\n    assert a in s, a[:40]\n    s=s.replace(a,b)\nopen('src/content/about.js','w').write(s)\nEOF\nnode tools/exit.mjs 2>&1 | tail -1 | cut -c1-100\nnode tools/build.mjs --verbose 2>&1 | tail -1 | cut -c150-\npgrep -af \"tests/run.mjs\" | while read p rest; do c=$(readlink /proc/$p/cwd 2>/dev/null); case \"$c\" in *xhigh.build-v2__20261105-162027*) echo \"mine still running: $p\";; esac; done; echo checked","description":"Update About answers, regenerate interview, rebuild","timeout":120000},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container