{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01JSikiTJgBJyXuHbuiBKr88","type":"tool_result","content":"15:## 1. The game\n51:## 2. Setting, cast, story\n85:## 3. Verified engine facts\n222:## 4. Architecture\n267:## 5. World\n338:## 6. Fire, wind, time, weather\n398:## 7. Player\n420:## 8. Weapons and wear\n452:## 9. The body\n474:## 10. Soldiers and AI\n508:## 11. Vehicles\n522:## 12. Buddies\n550:## 13. Stones, safehouses, side content\n590:## 14. Missions\n631:## 15. Writing\n663:## 16. UI and UX\n744:## 17. Dev mode\n787:## 18. Attract mode\n810:## 19. Multiplayer\n878:## 20. Art\n898:## 21. Animation\n923:## 22. Audio\n957:## 23. Packaging\n989:## 24. Testing\n1040:## 25. Build order\n1060:## 26. Cut order\n1078:## 27. Done, reports, coverage\ntests/suites/systems.mjs:212:    t.ok('surgery prompt below 20', g.state().prompts.some((x) => x.act === 'heal'));\ntests/suites/systems.mjs:257:  t.ok('tablet prompt', g.state().prompts.some((x) => x.act === 'tablet'));\ntests/suites/systems.mjs:470:  t.ok('halt prompt', g.state().prompts.some((x) => x.text === 'RAIL HALT'), JSON.stringify(g.state()\ntests/suites/systems.mjs:628:  // Settings: glyphs, persistence, defaults, music at 10%.\ntests/suites/systems.mjs:643:  // Device switch changes glyphs.\ntests/suites/systems.mjs:647:  t.eq('kbm glyph', g.state().prompts.find((x) => x.text === 'TEST')?.glyph, 'E');\ntests/suites/systems.mjs:650:  t.eq('PlayStation glyph', g.state().prompts.find((x) => x.text === 'TEST')?.glyph, 'SQUARE');\ntests/suites/systems.mjs:651:  g.settings.glyphs = 'xb'; e.step(2);\ntests/suites/systems.mjs:652:  t.eq('Xbox glyph', g.state().prompts.find((x) => x.text === 'TEST')?.glyph, 'X');\ntests/suites/systems.mjs:653:  t.eq('glyph set shown', g.state().glyphSet, 'xb');\ntests/suites/systems.mjs:654:  g.settings.glyphs = 'ps'; g.interact.clearTagged('tst');\ntests/suites/systems.mjs:655:  // Real presses, no bot: melee on F, next weapon on Triangle and the wheel, with no prompt showing.\ntests/suites/systems.mjs:854:  t.ok('take prompt', g.state().prompts.some((x) => /TAKE THE CASE/.test(x.text)), JSON.stringify(g.s\ntests/suites/systems.mjs:883:  t.ok('bank prompt', g.state().prompts.some((x) => /BANK/.test(x.text)));\n3795:### class SpringChain\n3796-\n3797-A chain of points hanging off a moving root. Call `update(dt, root, basis)` every frame\n3798-with the root's world position and its orientation (three columns: right, up, forward),\n3799-then read `points` (root first).\n3800-\n3801-- `new SpringChain(o: SpringChainOptions)`\n3802-- `readonly points: Vec3[]`\n3803-- `o: Required<SpringChainOptions>`\n3804-- `reset(root: Vec3, basis: readonly [Vec3, Vec3, Vec3]): void`: Put the chain straight out in its rest pose (no swing).\n3805-- `update(dt: number, root: Vec3, basis: readonly [Vec3, Vec3, Vec3]): void`\n3806-- `swing(basis: readonly [Vec3, Vec3, Vec3]): number`: How far the tip is from where the rest pose puts it (m): how much it is swinging.\n3807-\n3808-### interface SpringChainOptions\n3809-\n3810-- `segments: number`: Points after the root (≥ 1).\n3811-- `length: number`: Length of each segment (m).\n3812-- `rest?: Vec3`: Rest direction from the root in the root's own space (normalised; default straight back, −Z).\n3813-- `stiffness?: number`: Pull toward the rest pose per second (0 floppy … 30 stiff). Default 10.\n3814-- `keep?: number`: Velocity kept per 1/60 s (0..1). Default 0.94.\n3815-- `gravity?: number`: Gravity on the chain (m/s²). Default 6 (lighter than real: tails hold up a bit).\n3817:### class Squash\n3818-\n3819-Squash and stretch as a damped spring on `value` (0 = rest, + stretched, − squashed).\n3820-`scale()` turns it into a volume-preserving pair: `const [h, v] = squash.scale();\n3821-mesh.scale.set(h, v, h)`.\n3822-\n3823-- `value: number`\n3824-- `velocity: number`\n3825-- `stiffness: number`: Spring stiffness and damping (a critically damped spring has damping = 2√stiffness).\n3826-- `damping: number`\n3827-- `amount: number`: 0 turns it off; 2.5 is rubbery.\n3828-- `kick(v: number): void`: Add a kick: negative squashes (a landing), positive stretches (a jump).\n3829-- `set(v: number): void`: Set the shape directly (a held squash).\n3830-- `update(dt: number): void`\n3831-- `scale(out: [number, number] = [1, 1]): [number, number]`: [horizontal, vertical] scale: y = 1 + s, xz = 1 / √(1 + s), so the volume stays put.\n### twoBoneIK()\n\n```ts\nfunction twoBoneIK(root: Vec3, target: Vec3, a: number, b: number, pole: Vec3, out: Vec3 = [0, 0, 0]): Vec3\n```\n\nWhere the middle joint of a two-bone limb goes (a knee, an elbow) so the end reaches\n`target` from `root` with bones `a` and `b` long, bending toward `pole` (a point the knee\npoints at). Analytic (the law of cosines), no iterations; a target out of reach straightens\nthe limb toward it, one too close folds it as far as it goes. Returns the joint, into `out`.\n\n3648:### interface GaitSpec\n3649-\n3650-Procedural locomotion cycles with planted feet. Instead of posing every frame, describe\n3651-the gait (speed, cadence, stance, bounce, arm swing...) and the generator plants each\n3652-foot on the ground, sliding it backwards at exactly `speed` while it is in stance, then\n3653-swings it forward on an arc — heel strike, roll, toe-off included. Tweak numbers,\n3654-re-run `npm run anim -- check Walk`, look at the sheet.\n3655-\n3656-Phase: the RIGHT heel strikes at frame 0, the left at frames / 2.\n3657-\n3658-- `name: string`\n3659-- `frames: number`: One full cycle (two steps), frames at 30 fps.\n3660-- `speed: number`: Ground speed the cycle is authored for (m/s at playback rate 1).\n3661-- `stance: number`: Fraction of the cycle each foot is on the ground. Walk ≈ 0.55–0.6, run ≈ 0.3.\n3662-- `hip: number`: Mean pelvis height offset from rest (m); negative bends the knees.\n3663-- `bob?: number`: Pelvis bounce amplitude (m), twice per cycle.\n3664-- `low?: number`: Cycle fraction at which the pelvis is lowest (default: walk just after contact, run mid-stance).\n3665-- `squash?: number`: Squash at the lowest point (e.g. 0.05 = 5 % shorter, wider).\n3666-- `lift?: number`: How high the lowest point of the swinging foot clears the floor at its peak (m).\n3667-- `liftPeak?: number`: Where in the swing (0..1) the foot is highest (default 0.4).\n3668-- `reach?: number`: Shift the whole stride forward (m).\n3669-- `swingReach?: number`: Extra forward throw of the swinging foot late in the swing, before it settles (m).\n3670-- `swingDelay?: number`: Swing timing: 0 = even, + = the foot hangs back then whips forward (running).","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"71ec49de-27ff-45fb-a784-9f3cf302f915","uuid":"1a0b32c0-a2e7-4ae3-abb3-abcae19359b6","timestamp":"2026-11-06T03:40:34.063Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"15:## 1. The game\n51:## 2. Setting, cast, story\n85:## 3. Verified engine facts\n222:## 4. Architecture\n267:## 5. World\n338:## 6. Fire, wind, time, weather\n398:## 7. Player\n420:## 8. Weapons and wear\n452:## 9. The body\n474:## 10. Soldiers and AI\n508:## 11. Vehicles\n522:## 12. Buddies\n550:## 13. Stones, safehouses, side content\n590:## 14. Missions\n631:## 15. Writing\n663:## 16. UI and UX\n744:## 17. Dev mode\n787:## 18. Attract mode\n810:## 19. Multiplayer\n878:## 20. Art\n898:## 21. Animation\n923:## 22. Audio\n957:## 23. Packaging\n989:## 24. Testing\n1040:## 25. Build order\n1060:## 26. Cut order\n1078:## 27. Done, reports, coverage\ntests/suites/systems.mjs:212:    t.ok('surgery prompt below 20', g.state().prompts.some((x) => x.act === 'heal'));\ntests/suites/systems.mjs:257:  t.ok('tablet prompt', g.state().prompts.some((x) => x.act === 'tablet'));\ntests/suites/systems.mjs:470:  t.ok('halt prompt', g.state().prompts.some((x) => x.text === 'RAIL HALT'), JSON.stringify(g.state()\ntests/suites/systems.mjs:628:  // Settings: glyphs, persistence, defaults, music at 10%.\ntests/suites/systems.mjs:643:  // Device switch changes glyphs.\ntests/suites/systems.mjs:647:  t.eq('kbm glyph', g.state().prompts.find((x) => x.text === 'TEST')?.glyph, 'E');\ntests/suites/systems.mjs:650:  t.eq('PlayStation glyph', g.state().prompts.find((x) => x.text === 'TEST')?.glyph, 'SQUARE');\ntests/suites/systems.mjs:651:  g.settings.glyphs = 'xb'; e.step(2);\ntests/suites/systems.mjs:652:  t.eq('Xbox glyph', g.state().prompts.find((x) => x.text === 'TEST')?.glyph, 'X');\ntests/suites/systems.mjs:653:  t.eq('glyph set shown', g.state().glyphSet, 'xb');\ntests/suites/systems.mjs:654:  g.settings.glyphs = 'ps'; g.interact.clearTagged('tst');\ntests/suites/systems.mjs:655:  // Real presses, no bot: melee on F, next weapon on Triangle and the wheel, with no prompt showing.\ntests/suites/systems.mjs:854:  t.ok('take prompt', g.state().prompts.some((x) => /TAKE THE CASE/.test(x.text)), JSON.stringify(g.s\ntests/suites/systems.mjs:883:  t.ok('bank prompt', g.state().prompts.some((x) => /BANK/.test(x.text)));\n3795:### class SpringChain\n3796-\n3797-A chain of points hanging off a moving root. Call `update(dt, root, basis)` every frame\n3798-with the root's world position and its orientation (three columns: right, up, forward),\n3799-then read `points` (root first).\n3800-\n3801-- `new SpringChain(o: SpringChainOptions)`\n3802-- `readonly points: Vec3[]`\n3803-- `o: Required<SpringChainOptions>`\n3804-- `reset(root: Vec3, basis: readonly [Vec3, Vec3, Vec3]): void`: Put the chain straight out in its rest pose (no swing).\n3805-- `update(dt: number, root: Vec3, basis: readonly [Vec3, Vec3, Vec3]): void`\n3806-- `swing(basis: readonly [Vec3, Vec3, Vec3]): number`: How far the tip is from where the rest pose puts it (m): how much it is swinging.\n3807-\n3808-### interface SpringChainOptions\n3809-\n3810-- `segments: number`: Points after the root (≥ 1).\n3811-- `length: number`: Length of each segment (m).\n3812-- `rest?: Vec3`: Rest direction from the root in the root's own space (normalised; default straight back, −Z).\n3813-- `stiffness?: number`: Pull toward the rest pose per second (0 floppy … 30 stiff). Default 10.\n3814-- `keep?: number`: Velocity kept per 1/60 s (0..1). Default 0.94.\n3815-- `gravity?: number`: Gravity on the chain (m/s²). Default 6 (lighter than real: tails hold up a bit).\n3817:### class Squash\n3818-\n3819-Squash and stretch as a damped spring on `value` (0 = rest, + stretched, − squashed).\n3820-`scale()` turns it into a volume-preserving pair: `const [h, v] = squash.scale();\n3821-mesh.scale.set(h, v, h)`.\n3822-\n3823-- `value: number`\n3824-- `velocity: number`\n3825-- `stiffness: number`: Spring stiffness and damping (a critically damped spring has damping = 2√stiffness).\n3826-- `damping: number`\n3827-- `amount: number`: 0 turns it off; 2.5 is rubbery.\n3828-- `kick(v: number): void`: Add a kick: negative squashes (a landing), positive stretches (a jump).\n3829-- `set(v: number): void`: Set the shape directly (a held squash).\n3830-- `update(dt: number): void`\n3831-- `scale(out: [number, number] = [1, 1]): [number, number]`: [horizontal, vertical] scale: y = 1 + s, xz = 1 / √(1 + s), so the volume stays put.\n### twoBoneIK()\n\n```ts\nfunction twoBoneIK(root: Vec3, target: Vec3, a: number, b: number, pole: Vec3, out: Vec3 = [0, 0, 0]): Vec3\n```\n\nWhere the middle joint of a two-bone limb goes (a knee, an elbow) so the end reaches\n`target` from `root` with bones `a` and `b` long, bending toward `pole` (a point the knee\npoints at). Analytic (the law of cosines), no iterations; a target out of reach straightens\nthe limb toward it, one too close folds it as far as it goes. Returns the joint, into `out`.\n\n3648:### interface GaitSpec\n3649-\n3650-Procedural locomotion cycles with planted feet. Instead of posing every frame, describe\n3651-the gait (speed, cadence, stance, bounce, arm swing...) and the generator plants each\n3652-foot on the ground, sliding it backwards at exactly `speed` while it is in stance, then\n3653-swings it forward on an arc — heel strike, roll, toe-off included. Tweak numbers,\n3654-re-run `npm run anim -- check Walk`, look at the sheet.\n3655-\n3656-Phase: the RIGHT heel strikes at frame 0, the left at frames / 2.\n3657-\n3658-- `name: string`\n3659-- `frames: number`: One full cycle (two steps), frames at 30 fps.\n3660-- `speed: number`: Ground speed the cycle is authored for (m/s at playback rate 1).\n3661-- `stance: number`: Fraction of the cycle each foot is on the ground. Walk ≈ 0.55–0.6, run ≈ 0.3.\n3662-- `hip: number`: Mean pelvis height offset from rest (m); negative bends the knees.\n3663-- `bob?: number`: Pelvis bounce amplitude (m), twice per cycle.\n3664-- `low?: number`: Cycle fraction at which the pelvis is lowest (default: walk just after contact, run mid-stance).\n3665-- `squash?: number`: Squash at the lowest point (e.g. 0.05 = 5 % shorter, wider).\n3666-- `lift?: number`: How high the lowest point of the swinging foot clears the floor at its peak (m).\n3667-- `liftPeak?: number`: Where in the swing (0..1) the foot is highest (default 0.4).\n3668-- `reach?: number`: Shift the whole stride forward (m).\n3669-- `swingReach?: number`: Extra forward throw of the swinging foot late in the swing, before it settles (m).\n3670-- `swingDelay?: number`: Swing timing: 0 = even, + = the foot hangs back then whips forward (running).","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01JSikiTJgBJyXuHbuiBKr88","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
