{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgm5qtZ8zEJRrXUMfeL9p","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The stop check makes several points, and they don't all hold up, so I'll take each on evidence.\n\n**Worth acting on:**\n- The touch gate was never explicitly tested for prompts.\n- The tuned values: I should check whether each change is still needed. If a plan value can be restored, it should be.\n- \"Line by line\" is a fair ask. I can produce a real coverage table instead of just asserting it.\n\n**To verify rather than assume:** \"named sites were moved\". My earlier check flagged no sites, and the only thing I moved was fuel tanks, which the plan gives no coordinates for. I'll print exact numbers.\n\nI'll start by finding why each deviation exists."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3980,"cache_read_input_tokens":515305,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3980},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"71ec49de-27ff-45fb-a784-9f3cf302f915","uuid":"3cf6ec63-010c-4035-a50e-14283a0667ec","timestamp":"2026-11-06T05:00:24.522Z","request_id":"req_011Cgm5qtJ1ecN2uKrq68dLz"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgm5qtZ8zEJRrXUMfeL9p","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01C8YwgngEnzG6Kk14uMAeuS","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"echo \"--- sites and posts, exact offsets from the plan\"; cat > tools/tmp-sites.mjs <<'EOF'\nimport { SITES, POSTS } from '../src/content/sites.js';\nconst S = { 'mile-forty': [0, 40], 'pump-shed': [-120, 150], 'ranger-post': [40, -170], 'water-tower': [470, -180], 'fort-clement': [-430, -180], 'long-field': [-260, -300], granary: [400, 280], 'east-siding': [430, -60], 'three-wells': [-260, 240], 'pump-station': [-330, 395], 'salt-pan': [200, 470], 'the-cut': [150, -300], observatory: [-130, -520], 'the-pass': [-590, -430] };\nconst P = { p1: [90, -80], p2: [-200, 30], p3: [170, 90], p4: [-320, -90], p5: [280, -210], p6: [300, 390] };\nlet moved = 0;\nfor (const [k, at] of Object.entries(S)) { const a = (SITES[k] ?? SITES[k.replace('the-', '')]).at; const d = Math.hypot(a[0] - at[0], a[1] - at[1]); if (d) { moved++; console.log('MOVED', k, a, 'plan', at); } }\nfor (const [k, at] of Object.entries(P)) { const a = POSTS[k].at; const d = Math.hypot(a[0] - at[0], a[1] - at[1]); if (d) { moved++; console.log('MOVED', k, a, 'plan', at); } }\nconsole.log(`${Object.keys(S).length} sites, ${Object.keys(P).length} posts checked; ${moved} differ from the plan's coordinates`);\nprocess.exit(0);\nEOF\ntimeout 60 node tools/tmp-sites.mjs 2>&1 | grep -v '^`\\|WebGPURenderer\\|^file:\\|^ *\\^' | grep -v 'pixel-engine.js:' | cut -c1-120; rm -f tools/tmp-sites.mjs\necho \"--- M3 wind\"; grep -n \"id: 'm3'\" src/content/missions.js | cut -c1-200; grep -n -i \"wind\" tests/ISSUES.md | cut -c1-190; grep -n \"m3.*wind\\|wind.*m3\\|east-siding\\|tanks\" tests/suites/playthrough.mjs | cut -c1-170 | head -8; grep -n \"tanks:\" src/content/sites.js | cut -c1-170\necho \"--- fog\"; grep -n \"groundFog\" src/world/sky.js | cut -c1-170; grep -n \"function groundFog\"