{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgm8KGDctodL8GvTkp41c","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The check has a point on several items, and looking at them again I found I was wrong about one thing. I told you the HQ rule was unavoidable because \"both cannot hold for a first visit\". But the plan offers a second route: contracts can also be taken \"through the notice board in Mile Forty\", where you're safe. So the plan is consistent, and my neutrality rule isn't needed. I can fix that.\n\n**What I'll do:**\n1. **HQ:** follow the plan strictly (no pass means they shoot), and make sure the notice board really is a way in.\n2. **Last-act fever:** see if the plan's real behaviour works now that M9 hands you tablets, instead of exempting it.\n3. **M9's lines:** the plan says \"spoken\" lines, and three of the 16 are narration, so my count may simply be wrong.\n4. **Evidence:** replace source-grep rows with behaviour tests, and have the coverage tool read test names that actually ran and passed.\n\nThe fog `top` is different: −60 measurably destroys the picture, and the plan's own precedence rule covers it. I'll say so plainly rather than break the game to satisfy a number.\n\nFirst, the code involved."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3797,"cache_read_input_tokens":584357,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3797},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"71ec49de-27ff-45fb-a784-9f3cf302f915","uuid":"087bfc4e-a44a-4c36-b5a4-e8a8402fd5b7","timestamp":"2026-11-06T05:33:19.533Z","request_id":"req_011Cgm8KFoa24fVdmp7zh3BC"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgm8KGDctodL8GvTkp41c","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01WzLPQNiihZBtyjfpMgLu13","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"echo \"--- run.mjs t\"; sed -n 40,62p tests/run.mjs | cut -c1-150\necho \"--- board and offer\"; sed -n 162,170p src/ui/ui.js | cut -c1-190; grep -n \"  offer(\\|  start(\\|  accept(\\|  complete(\" src/missions/runner.js | cut -c1-120; n=$(grep -n \"  offer(\" src/missions/runner.js | cut -d: -f1); sed -n \"${n},$((n+16))p\" src/missions/runner.js | cut -c1-170; sed -n 212,224p src/missions/runner.js | cut -c1-150\necho \"--- End script\"; grep -n \"\\* end[A-Za-z]*(\\|\\* m9[A-Za-z]*(\" src/missions/scripts.js | cut -c1-90; n=$(grep -n \"\\* endWalk\\|\\* endPass\\|\\* end(\" src/missions/scripts.js | head -1 | cut -d: -f1); sed -n \"${n},$((n+30))p\" src/missions/scripts.js | cut -c1-140\ngrep -n \"steps:\" src/content/missions.js | sed -n '/end:/p' | cut -c1-300; sed -n 79,82p src/content/missions.js | cut -c1-320\necho \"--- spoken lines per mission\"; python3 - <<'EOF'\nimport re\ns=open('src/content/dialogue.js').read()\nc={};n={}\nfor k,v in re.findall(r\"^\\s*'((?:m\\d|end)[^']*)': \\[(.*)$\",s,re.M):\n    m=re.match(r'(m\\d|end)',k).group(1)\n    c[m]=c.get(m,0)+len(re.findall(r\"\\['[a-z]+', '\",v)); n[m]=n.get(m,0)+len(re.findall(r\"\\['', '\",v))\nprint('spoken',c); print('narration',n)\nEOF\ngrep -n \"chase\\|stepPatrols\\|  crew\\|crew:\" src/vehicles/driving.js | cut -c1-130 | head -5; sed -n 103,106p src/vehicles/vehicle.js | cut -c1-150\ngrep -n \"overnight\\|parked\\|repair(100\\|hp = 100\" src/game.js src/world/places.js src/vehicles/*.js | cut -c1-150 | head -4\ngrep -n \"birds\\|herds\\|gazelles\\|  flee\" src/actors/fauna.js | cut -c1-120 | head -6\ngrep -n \"sprites\\|batch\\|lightSlots\\|lights\\|\\.loop\\b\\|active\" src/world/fireview.js | cut -c1-120 | head -10\ngrep -n \"SKY\\|const TABLE\\|export\" src/world/s